    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Do you find yourself worrying a lot, even when there isn’t an obvious reason to?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Worrying? No, not really. I mean, I don't sit around chewing my nails or stressing out over nothing. If there's a problem, I just want to do something about it, you know? \n\nLike, we got this call last Tuesday for a cat stuck in a tree. Classic, right? You’d think people don’t actually call the station for that anymore, but this lady down on 4th street has this massive oak tree in her front yard. Beautiful tree, honestly. I’ve been thinking about planting an oak in my backyard, but the soil there is so clay-heavy, I don't know if the roots would take. I bought this aerator tool from Home Depot a few weeks ago to try and fix the lawn, but I lost the receipt and it's just sitting in my garage next to my old dirt bike. I really need to sell that bike, the carburetor is completely shot and I just never get around to it... \n\nWait, what were we talking about? Sorry. But yeah, worrying... no, I don't really get anxious or anything like that.",
