    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you had this kind of difficulty staying focused or getting organized since childhood?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, yeah, definitely. My mom says I was exactly like this back in grade school too. She always reminds me how I was constantly out of my seat, blurting out answers, losing my homework... just a total handful. She used to get all these notes sent home from my teachers saying I was bright enough to do the work, but I just wouldn't settle down. \n\nShe actually kept a bunch of those notes in this old shoebox. I saw it when I was helping her clean out her garage last summer. Man, her garage was a complete disaster. She had this old riding mower in there that hasn't run since like 2015. I told her I could probably fix it if I just cleaned the spark plugs and checked the fuel line, but you know how it is, trying to find the time. Plus, I usually just use a push mower for my yard anyway. It's better cardio, and honestly, I need it. I try to get a run in on my off days, but my left knee has been acting up ever since we had to haul all this heavy gear up three flights of stairs during a drill last month. \n\nWait, what did you ask me? Sorry. Oh, right, childhood. But yeah, my mom says I've basically always been this way.",
