      "doctor_question": "Have you ever been diagnosed with a thyroid problem?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Thyroid? No, not that I know of. My physicals for the department always come back clean, mostly. They're pretty strict about checking our bloodwork and all that, you know, because of the smoke exposure. Actually, my buddy Dave—he drives the tiller truck—he just found out he has high cholesterol and they put him on this crazy strict diet. Poor guy can't even look at a cheeseburger anymore. We used to hit up this diner on 5th Avenue after a long shift, they make these incredible patty melts. You know the kind with the rye bread and the caramelized onions? I tried making them at home once, but I burnt the onions. I always get impatient and turn the heat up too high. I just can't stand standing there stirring for twenty minutes. It's like, who has the time? I ended up just ordering a pizza instead. The pizza place near me has this really good hot honey pepperoni... \n\nAnyway, what were you asking? Oh, thyroid. No, I don't think so. Never been told I have a problem with it.",
