    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Do you spend a lot of time worrying that there is something seriously wrong with your health?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Worry about my health? No, not really. Like I said, the department keeps pretty close tabs on us anyway, so I figure if something was wrong, they'd catch it. I feel fine, mostly. I mean, besides that knee thing I mentioned. \n\nI actually tried using the rowing machine at the station yesterday to take it easy on the joints, but the digital monitor on it is totally busted. It just flashes 88:88 constantly. It's so distracting. I told the captain we should just order a new one, maybe one of those fancy ones with the water resistance? I saw a commercial for those when I was up late the other night. I couldn't sleep because my neighbor's dog wouldn't stop barking. It's this little terrier mix—cute, but man, it has a set of lungs on it. I almost went over there to say something, but it was like 2 AM, and I didn't want to be that guy, you know? Plus, I had to be up at 5 for a shift anyway, so I just put on a podcast to drown it out. It was this really interesting one about how they used to build ships in the 1700s, with all the tar and the wood bending... \n\nWait, sorry, what did you ask me? I totally lost my train of thought. Oh, right, worrying about getting sick. Yeah, no, I don't really stress about that kind of stuff at all.",
