      "doctor_question": "Did you have these same attention or restlessness problems in more than one setting, like at home and at school or work?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Yeah, I guess it's pretty much everywhere. Like I said, at school I was always getting in trouble for being out of my seat, and at home my mom was always on my case about my room being a disaster or me not finishing my chores. Even now at the firehouse, the guys are always giving me grief because I start cleaning the rig, and then I notice a loose bolt on the ladder, so I go get the toolbox, but then I see the air tanks need refilling, and next thing you know, the rig is half-washed, the toolbox is sitting out, and I'm off doing something else. \n\nIt's actually kind of funny, my buddy Dave—the one with the cholesterol—he calls me the \"Tasmanian Devil\" because I just blow through a room and leave a trail of half-finished projects. Speaking of Dave, he actually brought in these turkey burgers the other day to try and stick to his diet, and they were... well, they were terrible. Dry as a bone. I felt bad for the guy, so I tried to show him how to mix in some Greek yogurt and a little bit of feta cheese to keep them moist. I saw that trick on a cooking show once. It was one of those weekend marathon things, you know? They had this whole segment on grilling, and they showed how to make these cedar-plank salmon fillets that looked amazing. I actually bought some cedar planks to try it, but they're still sitting in my trunk. I keep forgetting to bring them inside. My trunk is a mess right now, honestly. I've got my turnout gear, my gym bag, the cedar planks, and like three empty water bottles rolling around in there. \n\nWhat were we talking about? Oh, right, the attention stuff. But yeah, it's definitely not just at work or just at home. It's kind of a full-time thing for me.",
